# An extension Cra loads from its own Extensions/ folder (an import from Arc, Dia or Chrome, or Add Unpacked
# Extension…), removed in chrome://extensions, stays removed. Chromium's Remove deletes only its record of an
# extension loaded with --load-extension, so the next launch loaded the folder again: it could be turned off but
# not removed (a review, 17 Nov 2026). The removal now takes the folder out of that profile.
budget rss=600
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/Extension
relaunch
cra://open?url=chrome://extensions/?id=${EXTENSION_ID}
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"chrome.management.uninstall('${EXTENSION_ID}',{showConfirmDialog:true}).catch(()=>0);'asked'","userGesture":true}
expect-log Chromium dialog [0-9]+ shown over window
# Chromium ignores a press in the first moments a dialog shows (its input protection).
wait 1
cra://debug?chromiumDialogs=Remove
expect-log Chromium dialog pressed Remove
expect-log extension Extension was removed from Default; it stops loading there
relaunch
cra://open?url=chrome://extensions/?id=${EXTENSION_ID}
wait 3
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"chrome.management.getAll().then(a=>a.map(e=>e.id).includes('${EXTENSION_ID}')?'came back after relaunch':'still removed after relaunch')","awaitPromise":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*(came back|still removed) after relaunch
reject-log came back after relaunch
